<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burna-Buriash II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1359–1333 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burna-Buriash II was a Kassite king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> in the 14th century BCE. Several of his letters to the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaohs</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhenaten">Akhenaten</a> and Tutankhamun survive among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>, in which he exchanged gifts, demanded gold and arranged royal marriages. He married a daughter of the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashur-uballit-i">Ashur-uballit I</a>, tying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> to the rising power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>.</p></div>
